OctoSnap is a lightweight Qt6 graphical user interface for NetBSD's
file system snapshots (fss(4) / fssconfig(8)), allowing administrators
to manage FFS snapshots.

Features:
- List snapshots with unit, mount point, backing-store size and state
- Create and destroy snapshots (optionally removing the backing store)
- Mount snapshots read-only for file inspection and unmount them
- Privilege separation: a minimal, allow-listed helper runs as root
  through doas(1) or sudo(8); the GUI never runs as root
- Built-in theme switcher and internationalization (en, pt_BR)
